    "verdict": "NOT a router bug. The deterministic soft-prior router (centroid cosine + softmax) is 0.194ms p50 — three orders of magnitude below the ~542ms figure. That lumped baseline metric was router_ms = embed_query + routing, dominated ENTIRELY by the bge GPU query embed. Sub-stage split (p50): embed 535.1ms >> sparse_bm25 71.2ms > centroid_score 5.8ms > dense 2.5ms > rrf 1.2ms ~ cutoff 1.2ms > router 0.19ms > payload 0.02ms. FINDING: the query EMBED is the retrieval bottleneck (86%% of the 620ms total) AND it is GPU-state-variable — 535ms here (warm, retrieval-only) vs ~165ms in the arch-baseline-v2 run — so embed latency is unstable, not fixed. Optimization targets (for Dok/W3.3, NOT changed here): fp16/quantized or smaller embedder, keep-GPU-warm / avoid downclock, batch where possible. Second cost = BM25 sparse (71ms). The routing logic itself needs no work."
